# Motion

Motion explains state, origin, or feedback. A transition that only decorates the screen does not ship.

- Enter with ease-out over about 200ms. Exit about 20% shorter, 160ms.
- Menus and dropdowns use 150–250ms. Popovers begin near scale 0.95 and move from the trigger back toward the trigger.
- Pressed controls scale to about 0.97. A moving knob may stretch about 12%.
- Stagger related rows by about 30ms. Shared elements reuse one layout id.
- Everyday UI does not bounce. Held elements are not continuously tweened.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity`. Avoid layout-affecting properties on large lists and charts.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` by cutting the transition to instant.

Tokens and the full motion notes are in `docs/design/tokens.css` and `docs/design/motion-guidelines.md`.
